# Copy to `server/.env` and fill in what you need. Gitignored.
# Anything already set in the environment wins, so the app's own PORT /
# ADMIN_TOKEN / CONFIG_DB are never overridden from here.
#
# See docs/integrations.md for what each of these is and how to get one.

# --- GitHub -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed if you've run `gh auth login` on this machine.
# GH_TOKEN=

# --- Slack ------------------------------------------------------------------
# A user token (xoxp-) sees your DMs and private channels and posts as you;
# a bot token (xoxb-) only sees what it's been invited to, and can't search
# at all — so the recent-messages feed needs xoxp-.
# SLACK_TOKEN=
#
# Conversations the feed should skip, in case Slack won't tell us what you've
# muted (the endpoint that knows isn't a public one). Merged with whatever it
# does manage to report.
# SLACK_MUTED=C0123ABCD,C0456EFGH

# --- Claude -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to set for the CLI itself: sessions run locally through `claude`, as
# whoever it is already signed in as on this machine.
#
# These two are for the sessions a *changeset* starts. Such a session runs in a
# worktree, which is a directory `claude` has never seen, so it gets none of the
# MCP servers configured for the repository it came from — and an agent pointed
# at a note it cannot read is no use. The answer is a `.mcp.json` committed at
# the repository's root, which a worktree inherits along with every other
# tracked file, expanding these:
#
#   PENSIVE_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000/<sourceId>/mcp
#   PENSIVE_MCP_TOKEN=
#
# They live here rather than in the file because the second is a source token,
# and a repository that gets pushed is the wrong place for one. The session
# inherits this server's environment, which is what makes the indirection work.
# An unset variable expands to nothing, so a machine that hasn't set them has a
# session with no notes rather than one that won't start.

# --- Server -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Settable here too, for a server started by hand rather than by the app.
# PORT=4000
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# ADMIN_TOKEN=
# CONFIG_DB=./data/config.db
